+
+## Open bounded peer finding — `review-7b6e9833ed831a81`
+
+The current source (`174ca5baed3dbde7440f328eef878698ce4ca98b9424621bff29c5f6f77abe76`)
+admits a three-demo lesson in which an undeclared rival fits every visible
+demonstration and changes the query. The rival selects, independently per row,
+the **longest** compatible period that exposes at least one repeated residue
+(`1 <= p <= R`), then extends that period. The authority selects the shortest.
+
+Replay `generate(7, i, difficulty="medium")` for indices `i=0,1,2` as demos
+and `i=3` as query. Every demo active row has only one compatible repeated
+period. Query row 3 (zero-based) has prefix `[4,6,0,4,4,6,0,4]`, compatible with
+periods 4 and 7. The authority chooses 4; the rival chooses 7 and differs at
+columns 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, and 14. The current `lesson_identifiable` hook returns
+no reasons because this rival is absent from its declared set. This is a
+demonstration-identifiability gap for a plausible rival, not a mislabeled grid.
+
+The bounded search covered 192 generated grids and 96 three-demo windows
+(seeds 0..31, indices 0..5, medium difficulty, starts 0..2). This rival fit all
+demos in 14 windows and changed the query in 4. A second rival that treats
+leading zeros as a preserved margin fit all 96 windows and changed no query.
+All 192 inputs passed `self_check`; all 96 current lesson hooks passed. The
+longest-period rival also fits the three canonical training pairs but differs
+on the canonical test pair. It therefore is not a canonical shortcut under the
+existing all-labeled-pairs definition.
+
+Protected Racket execution confirmed all four canonical labels and the four
+generated witness labels: 8 rule applications, all agreeing with the Python
+parity solver. Exact rule SHA-256:
+`7278144d22eaa349ae7e24bf6ab2f771d19577b1f1fa66513c54d79861440c22`;
+normalized rule hash `4cb32d01d908`. No generator, authority, or evidence-index
+change was made. A possible follow-up is to add this lesson competitor and
+ensure demonstrations distinguish shortest from longer compatible periods.
+
+Evidence in this return: `WORK/checks/80271cb9b303/probe.py`, `result.json`, and
+`command-retry.json`. From the packet outer directory, replay with
+`WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run --receipt checks/80271cb9b303/command-replay.json python3 ../checks/80271cb9b303/probe.py`.
+The original `command.json` records a probe-only property/call error before any
+rule application; the corrected retry exited 0. The result is source-bound,
+finite reviewer evidence only, with no broad battery or acceptance claim.
+
+An additional eight protected native calls replayed only those same retained
+inputs through the exact canonical program with its period candidates reordered
+to longest repeated period first (full-prefix fallback retained). Native rival
+outputs matched the Python rival on 8/8 inputs; both canonical and generated
+four-pair authority-match vectors were `[true,true,true,false]`. The exact rival
+program and outputs are in `WORK/checks/80271cb9b303/rival-native-result.json`,
+with executable `rival_native.py` and successful `rival-native-command.json`.
+This adds native rival parity evidence; the original search and eight authority
+executions remain separately recorded in the unchanged `result.json`.
